2. didder (Docker image only)
-----------------------------

This repository does not contain didder's source code. The application runs
didder as a separate program (a subprocess) and does not link against it.

The Docker image built from this repository's Dockerfile does include a
didder binary, compiled from:

    https://github.com/makeworld-the-better-one/didder
    commit 408a18aef878b456fe5cdbec406070fd5bd5c2d2 (see DIDDER_REF in the
    Dockerfile)

didder is Copyright (c) makeworld and contributors and is licensed under the
GNU General Public License, version 3 (GPL-3.0). Its license text is shipped
in the image at /usr/share/licenses/didder/LICENSE, and the corresponding
source code is available at the URL and commit above. If you distribute the
image, the GPL-3.0 terms apply to the didder binary it contains.

The didder binary also statically includes Go libraries under their own
licenses, including github.com/makeworld-the-better-one/dither (MPL-2.0),
github.com/urfave/cli (MIT), github.com/disintegration/imaging (MIT) and
golang.org/x/image (BSD-3-Clause); their sources are pinned by didder's
go.mod/go.sum at the commit above.


